# FEATURE-DOCTOR-TRUSTED-ANDROID-DEVICE-LOCK-1 Phase 1 — durable rules

Phase 1 of the trusted-device programme ships the two **device-independent**
Doctor restrictions. It deliberately contains no Android app, no device
registry and no login device lock — those are Phases 2–4 and are blocked on
clinic hardware that does not exist yet.

## 1. One authority

`App\Modules\RME\Services\DoctorRoomScopeService` is the ONLY authority for
both restrictions. Do not add a parallel room-scope or print-deny check.

"Is this a scoped Doctor" is delegated to
`DoctorPatientScopeService::shouldApplyDoctorScope()` so there is exactly one
definition — **Owner / Super Admin / Supervisor RME stay exempt**, and Perawat,
Admin Klinik and Kasir are never room-scoped by this rule.

## 2. The room is server-side, never a request value

The doctor's current room is read from the live online context
(`trx_user_online_contexts`, `role_context = doctor`, `status = online`,
Sprint 66.0 `startDoctorSession`). A context that is offline, inactive,
non-doctor, or roomless resolves to `null`.

Never trust `clinic_room_id`, `branch_id`, `visit_id` or `patient_id` from the
request. A scoped Doctor's room/branch list filters are dropped in the
controller, so there is no "Semua Ruangan" capability.

## 3. The ACTIVE set only — history is never restricted

The restriction applies **only** to `ClinicVisit::PRE_EXAM_STATUSES`
(`registered` / `waiting` / `in_progress`) — exactly the set the room worklist
and patient queue show.

`cashier_pending` (post-examination) and `completed` / `cancelled` (historical)
are **never** room-restricted. A doctor must always be able to read back the
records they created, so:

- `applyRoomScope()` narrows active rows only and leaves every other status
  visible. It must NOT emit a bare `where('clinic_room_id', …)`, because the
  same closure also feeds Daftar Kunjungan (`ClinicVisitService::paginate`),
  which lists historical visits.
- `deniesActiveVisitOutsideRoom()` returns false for any non-`PRE_EXAM` status.

These two must stay mirror images of each other: **hiding a row and denying a
direct URL are the same rule.** If you change one, change both.

## 4. Fail closed, but only on the active set

No resolvable room ⇒ the doctor sees and may open **no ACTIVE visit**
(`whereNotIn(PRE_EXAM_STATUSES)` in listings, deny in the policy). History
stays readable. Never fail *open*.

## 5. Denial is server-side; the sidebar and hidden buttons are not security

Room isolation is enforced in `ClinicVisitPolicy` (`view` / `update` /
`transition` / `print`) and `OdontogramPolicy`.

`completeExamination` is deliberately NOT room-guarded: the HTTP path authorises
`transition` (room-guarded) first, and the ability is re-checked inside
`ClinicVisitService::transitionStatus()`. Guarding it too would strand a doctor
whose online context lapsed mid-encounter — availability cost, no security gain.
Do not "fix" this by adding the guard.
`MedicalRecordController@show` authorises `view` on the **opened** visit before
the Sprint 64.0 canonical redirect, so the RME surface is covered without
touching the patient-centric workspace resolver.

## 6. Doctor may read and edit, never print

`print` is denied for a scoped Doctor on:

- `rme.visits.print`, `rme.visits.pdf` (`ClinicVisitPolicy::print`)
- `rme.odontograms.print` (`OdontogramPolicy::print`)

Both Blade actions are already wrapped in `@can('print', …)`, so the policy
denial hides the buttons automatically — do not add a separate UI-only check.
Prescription printing is **out of scope** and must keep working.

Existing RME/Odontogram read + edit lifecycle (consent gate, room gate,
finalisation, historical immutability) is unchanged. Non-Doctor roles that can
print today must keep printing.

## 7. Audit real attempts only, from controllers

Audit from the **controller**, never from a policy: policies are also evaluated
for `@can` UI gating, and auditing there would record a "rejection" every time a
button is merely hidden.

Events: `DOCTOR_ROOM_ACCESS_REJECTED`, `DOCTOR_PRINT_RME_REJECTED`,
`DOCTOR_PRINT_ODONTOGRAM_REJECTED` — written through the shared
`AuditLogService` (`sys_audit_logs`). Payload is identifiers and status only:
never patient PII, never KTP/NIK.

## 8. Out of scope for Phase 1 (do not silently add)

Android app, kiosk/Device Owner provisioning, cryptographic device identity,
`Master Data → Device Dokter`, and the Doctor login device lock. Those need
real clinic hardware and a signing-key governance decision, and enabling login
enforcement with zero registered devices would lock every doctor out of the
live pilot.
